cartridge "GRENOUILLE/JEAN-FRANCOIS SEHAN/1984"

' GRENOUILLE - ColecoVision version of the Oric game by Jean-Francois Sehan
' ("L'Oric a l'affiche", Editions du P.S.I., 1984, pp. 8-14). Adapted by
' Amy & Claude, Amy Studio 2026. Built by build.py from this file,
' ../_common/amy/core.alexis, pages.txt, art.py and music/*.txt.
'
' THE GAME (as in the book): the frog dreams it must cross a road (4 lanes
' of cars and trucks) and a river (4 lanes of logs and crocodiles) to reach
' the five rocks of the far bank. Lanes move in alternate directions. On the
' road, touching a vehicle is fatal; on the river, the frog must stand on a
' log or a crocodile and drifts with it; carried off the side = lost. A
' rock can only be taken once. Five rocks = a new round (+50). Points: +1 a
' hop forward, +10 a rock. Three frogs.
'
' CONTROLS: joystick left/right = side hop, up or either button = hop
' forward (the book's space bar), down = hop back. Title: up/down choose,
' left/right change the start level, a button confirms.
'
' LIBERTIES (listed for Amy):
' - Smooth lanes: every lane scrolls by whole pixels (pre-shifted tiles, see
'   art.py) instead of 6-pixel characters; the frog hops smoothly (16 px
'   forward in 8 frames, 8 px sideways in 4 frames).
' - A hop back (down) is allowed (the book had none); +1 point only for a
'   new best row on each trip, so hopping back and forth earns nothing.
' - One stop on the middle bank (the book had two rows there): the screen
'   has 24 rows, the safe area 22.
' - Levels: each round of five rocks is a level; the lanes get faster level
'   by level (speeds measured with model/frogsim.c for fairness). A frog is
'   given back at each new level (at most 5). The title lets you start at
'   level 1-9.
' - A fly sometimes rests on a free rock: taking that rock gives +50.
' - The frog is lost when its centre leaves the safe area (book: X<3, X>36).
' - Colour, animation, music and sound effects are new.

' screen third 0: 150 tiles in 2 runs (generated by art.py)
